    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-sample/q12",
      "question": "<p>A student was asked to give the exact solution to the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2^{2x+4} - 9(2^x) = 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>The student’s attempt is shown below:</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2^{2x+4} - 9(2^x) = 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"2^{2x} + 2^4 - 9(2^x) = 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>Let <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2^x = y\"></span></p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y^2 - 9y + 8 = 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(y - 8)(y - 1) = 0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y = 8 \\text{ or } y = 1\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x = 3\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x = 0\"></span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Identify the two errors made by the student.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) Find the exact solution to the equation.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
