    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-sample/q13",
      "question": "<p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Factorise completely <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^3 + 10x^2 + 25x\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) Sketch the curve with equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y = x^3 + 10x^2 + 25x\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>showing the coordinates of the points at which the curve cuts or touches the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>The point with coordinates <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-3, 0)\"></span> lies on the curve with equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y = (x + a)^3 + 10(x + a)^2 + 25(x + a)\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> is a constant.</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) Find the two possible values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p>",
