    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-sample/q14",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:142mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-sample/q14-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 2. Population model on a logarithmic scale.\"></figure><p>A town’s population, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>, is modelled by the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P = ab^t\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> are constants and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> is the number of years since the population was first recorded.</p><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> shown in Figure 2 illustrates the linear relationship between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\log_{10} P\"></span> for the population over a period of 100 years.</p><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> meets the vertical axis at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0, 5)\"></span> as shown. The gradient of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{1}{200}\"></span>.</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(a) Write down an equation for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(b) Find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(4)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(c) With reference to the model interpret</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(i) the value of the constant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span>,</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(ii) the value of the constant <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(d) Find</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(i) the population predicted by the model when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t = 100\"></span>, giving your answer to the nearest hundred thousand,</p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(ii) the number of years it takes the population to reach 200,000, according to the model.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p class=\"exam-subpart\">(e) State two reasons why this may not be a realistic population model.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p>",
      "steps": [
