    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-sample/q15",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:113mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-sample/q15-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 3. Curves C1 and C2.\"></figure><p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_1\"></span>, shown in Figure 3, has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = 4x^2 - 6x + 4\"></span>.</p><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\\left(\\frac{1}{2}, 2\\right)\"></span> lies on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_1\"></span>.</p><p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_2\"></span>, also shown in Figure 3, has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = \\frac{1}{2}x + \\ln(2x)\"></span>.</p><p>The normal to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_1\"></span> at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span> meets <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_2\"></span> at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span>.</p><p>Find the exact coordinates of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"Q\"></span>.</p><p>(Solutions based entirely on graphical or numerical methods are not acceptable.)</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(8)</span></p>",
